   "subject": "Mark-recapture observer performance limits",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Greetings List,</div><div><br></div><div>I&#39;m working on some aerial survey data for marine mammals with independent observers. Is there a limit to which the MR model will deal with poor observer performance?  In this situation, the primary observers are experienced professionals and the secondary observers are locals. When I look at the graphs depicting observer performance (e.g. objects detected by either observer compared to observer x, for binned distances) the primary observer performance looks great while the secondary is lacking: 444 obs by primary, 114 obs by secondary and 85 by both. When I run the analysis, the MR model assigns a similar dismal probability of detection to both observers (~0.30 each and ~0.50 combined). Is the poor secondary observer performance precluding the use of this data for MR analysis?  As a 0.30 detection probability is unlikely for the primary observer (as evidenced by other survey data), it would appear that the MR analysis will give the data a positive bias? Is there a &#39;rule of thumb&#39; to assess observer performance when using MR analysis?</div><div><br></div><div>Thanks in advance,</div><div></div><div>Mitch Firman   <br></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "ZJ76vrVKAQAJ",
   "from": "Eric Rexstad",
   "author": "f2122b34f1aa6e95",
   "date": "2020-03-01T13:33:15Z",
   "subject": "Re: [distance-sampling] Mark-recapture observer performance limits",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div>\r\n<div>Mitch</div>\r\n<br>\r\n<div>Prof Borchers offers the following suggestion.  Place &quot;observer&quot; as a covariate in the mrmodel.\r\n<font style=\"font-size:14.5px\"><font style=\"font-family:Nylas-Pro,Helvetica,&quot;Lucidia Grande&quot;,sans-serif\"> If you don’t explicitly put observer in, you are fitting a model in which the primary and secondary observers’ detection functions are constrained to\r\n be the same.</font></font></div>\r\n<div><br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div><font style=\"font-size:14.5px\"><font style=\"font-family:Nylas-Pro,Helvetica,&quot;Lucidia Grande&quot;,sans-serif\">Here’s an example got by modifying some code in the file “mrds-golftees-distill.Rmd” file that is available on the distance sampling site:</font></font></div>\r\n<div><a href=\"http://examples.distancesampling.org/mrds-golftees/mrds-golftees-distill.Rmd\" title=\"http://examples.distancesampling.org/mrds-golftees/mrds-golftees-distill.Rmd\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://examples.distancesampling.org/mrds-golftees/mrds-golftees-distill.Rmd&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792473517542000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2XuwhJhTrgRuOrPO_cfCvZ\"><font style=\"font-size:14.5px\"><font style=\"font-family:Nylas-Pro,Helvetica,&quot;Lucidia Grande&quot;,sans-serif\">http://examples.distancesampling.org/mrds-golftees/mrds-golftees-distill.Rmd</font></font></a><font style=\"font-size:14.5px\"><font style=\"font-family:Nylas-Pro,Helvetica,&quot;Lucidia Grande&quot;,sans-serif\"> \r\n Note the comments included in the code below.  Specifically, note the first analysis produces identical p0 estimates for each observer, the second analysis produces observer-specific estimates.</font></font></div>\r\n<div><br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div><font style=\"font-size:14.5px\"><font style=\"font-family:Nylas-Pro,Helvetica,&quot;Lucidia Grande&quot;,sans-serif\"><font style=\"font-family:Courier New\"><font style=\"font-size:11px\">&gt; # fit IO model without observer</font></font></font></font></div>\r\n<div><font style=\"font-size:14.5px\"><font style=\"font-family:Nylas-Pro,Helvetica,&quot;Lucidia Grande&quot;,sans-serif\"><font style=\"font-family:Courier New\"><font style=\"font-size:11px\">&gt; io.fi.dist &lt;- ddf(method=&#39;</font></font></font></font><font style=\"font-size:14.5px\"><font style=\"font-family:Nylas-Pro,Helvetica,&quot;Lucidia Grande&quot;,sans-serif\"><font style=\"font-family:Courier New\"><font style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"color:rgb(16,129,247)\"><a href=\"http://io.fi\" title=\"http://io.fi\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://io.fi&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792473517542000&amp;usg=AOvVaw12Rmv9E0oR4bMp5x0ASIYk\">io.fi</a></span></font></font></font></font><font style=\"font-size:14.5px\"><font style=\"font-family:Nylas-Pro,Helvetica,&quot;Lucidia Grande&quot;,sans-serif\"><font style=\"font-family:Courier New\"><font style=\"font-size:11px\">&#39;,\r\n mrmodel=~glm(link=&#39;logit&#39;,formula=~distance), data=detections, meta.data=list(width=4))</font></font></font></font></div>\r\n<div><font style=\"font-size:14.5px\"><font style=\"font-family:Nylas-Pro,Helvetica,&quot;Lucidia Grande&quot;,sans-serif\"><font style=\"font-family:Courier New\"><font style=\"font-size:11px\">&gt; </font></font></font></font></div>\r\n<div><font style=\"font-size:14.5px\"><font style=\"font-family:Nylas-Pro,Helvetica,&quot;Lucidia Grande&quot;,sans-serif\"><font style=\"font-family:Courier New\"><font style=\"font-size:11px\">&gt; # fit IO model WITH observer</font></font></font></font></div>\r\n<div><font style=\"font-size:14.5px\"><font style=\"font-family:Nylas-Pro,Helvetica,&quot;Lucidia Grande&quot;,sans-serif\"><font style=\"font-family:Courier New\"><font style=\"font-size:11px\">&gt; io.fi.dist_obs &lt;- ddf(method=&#39;</font></font></font></font><font style=\"font-size:14.5px\"><font style=\"font-family:Nylas-Pro,Helvetica,&quot;Lucidia Grande&quot;,sans-serif\"><font style=\"font-family:Courier New\"><font style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"color:rgb(16,129,247)\"><a href=\"http://io.fi\" title=\"http://io.fi\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://io.fi&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792473517542000&amp;usg=AOvVaw12Rmv9E0oR4bMp5x0ASIYk\">io.fi</a></span></font></font></font></font><font style=\"font-size:14.5px\"><font style=\"font-family:Nylas-Pro,Helvetica,&quot;Lucidia Grande&quot;,sans-serif\"><font style=\"font-family:Courier New\"><font style=\"font-size:11px\">&#39;,\r\n mrmodel=~glm(link=&#39;logit&#39;,formula=~distance+observer), data=detections, meta.data=list(width=4))</font></font></font></font></div>\r\n<div><font style=\"font-size:14.5px\"><font style=\"font-family:Nylas-Pro,Helvetica,&quot;Lucidia Grande&quot;,sans-serif\"><font style=\"font-family:Courier New\"><font style=\"font-size:11px\">&gt; </font></font></font></font></div>\r\n<div><font style=\"font-size:14.5px\"><font style=\"font-family:Nylas-Pro,Helvetica,&quot;Lucidia Grande&quot;,sans-serif\"><font style=\"font-family:Courier New\"><font style=\"font-size:11px\">&gt; # Look at output for IO model without observer</font></font></font></font></div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div><font style=\"font-size:14.5px\"><font style=\"font-family:Nylas-Pro,Helvetica,&quot;Lucidia Grande&quot;,sans-serif\"><font style=\"font-family:Courier New\"><font style=\"font-size:11px\">&gt; # Note that &quot;Average primary p(0)&quot; and “Average secondary p(0)” estimates are\r\n identical</font></font></font></font></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div><font style=\"font-size:14.5px\"><font style=\"font-family:Nylas-Pro,Helvetica,&quot;Lucidia Grande&quot;,sans-serif\"><font style=\"font-family:Courier New\"><font style=\"font-size:11px\">&gt; # -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------</font></font></font></font></div>\r\n<div><font style=\"font-size:14.5px\"><font style=\"font-family:Nylas-Pro,Helvetica,&quot;Lucidia Grande&quot;,sans-serif\"><font style=\"font-family:Courier New\"><font style=\"font-size:11px\">&gt; io.fi.dist</font></font></font></font></div>\r\n<div><br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div><font style=\"font-size:14.5px\"><font style=\"font-family:Nylas-Pro,Helvetica,&quot;Lucidia Grande&quot;,sans-serif\"><font style=\"font-family:Courier New\"><font style=\"font-size:11px\">Distance sampling analysis object</font></font></font></font></div>\r\n<div><br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div><font style=\"font-size:14.5px\"><font style=\"font-family:Nylas-Pro,Helvetica,&quot;Lucidia Grande&quot;,sans-serif\"><font style=\"font-family:Courier New\"><font style=\"font-size:11px\">Summary for </font></font></font></font><font style=\"font-size:14.5px\"><font style=\"font-family:Nylas-Pro,Helvetica,&quot;Lucidia Grande&quot;,sans-serif\"><font style=\"font-family:Courier New\"><font style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"color:rgb(16,129,247)\"><a href=\"http://io.fi\" title=\"http://io.fi\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://io.fi&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792473517542000&amp;usg=AOvVaw12Rmv9E0oR4bMp5x0ASIYk\">io.fi</a></span></font></font></font></font><font style=\"font-size:14.5px\"><font style=\"font-family:Nylas-Pro,Helvetica,&quot;Lucidia Grande&quot;,sans-serif\"><font style=\"font-family:Courier New\"><font style=\"font-size:11px\"> object </font></font></font></font></div>\r\n<div><font style=\"font-size:14.5px\"><font style=\"font-family:Nylas-Pro,Helvetica,&quot;Lucidia Grande&quot;,sans-serif\"><font style=\"font-family:Courier New\"><font style=\"font-size:11px\">Number of observations   :  162 </font></font></font></font></div>\r\n<div><font style=\"font-size:14.5px\"><font style=\"font-family:Nylas-Pro,Helvetica,&quot;Lucidia Grande&quot;,sans-serif\"><font style=\"font-family:Courier New\"><font style=\"font-size:11px\">Number seen by primary   :  124 </font></font></font></font></div>\r\n<div><font style=\"font-size:14.5px\"><font style=\"font-family:Nylas-Pro,Helvetica,&quot;Lucidia Grande&quot;,sans-serif\"><font style=\"font-family:Courier New\"><font style=\"font-size:11px\">Number seen by secondary :  142 </font></font></font></font></div>\r\n<div><font style=\"font-size:14.5px\"><font style=\"font-family:Nylas-Pro,Helvetica,&quot;Lucidia Grande&quot;,sans-serif\"><font style=\"font-family:Courier New\"><font style=\"font-size:11px\">Number seen by both      :  104 </font></font></font></font></div>\r\n<div><font style=\"font-size:14.5px\"><font style=\"font-family:Nylas-Pro,Helvetica,&quot;Lucidia Grande&quot;,sans-serif\"><font style=\"font-family:Courier New\"><font style=\"font-size:11px\">AIC                      :  701.3888 </font></font></font></font></div>\r\n<div><br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div><br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div><font style=\"font-size:14.5px\"><font style=\"font-family:Nylas-Pro,Helvetica,&quot;Lucidia Grande&quot;,sans-serif\"><font style=\"font-family:Courier New\"><font style=\"font-size:11px\">Conditional detection function parameters:</font></font></font></font></div>\r\n<div><font style=\"font-size:14.5px\"><font style=\"font-family:Nylas-Pro,Helvetica,&quot;Lucidia Grande&quot;,sans-serif\"><font style=\"font-family:Courier New\"><font style=\"font-size:11px\">              estimate        se</font></font></font></font></div>\r\n<div><font style=\"font-size:14.5px\"><font style=\"font-family:Nylas-Pro,Helvetica,&quot;Lucidia Grande&quot;,sans-serif\"><font style=\"font-family:Courier New\"><font style=\"font-size:11px\">(Intercept)  2.8806278 0.3846499</font></font></font></font></div>\r\n<div><font style=\"font-size:14.5px\"><font style=\"font-family:Nylas-Pro,Helvetica,&quot;Lucidia Grande&quot;,sans-serif\"><font style=\"font-family:Courier New\"><font style=\"font-size:11px\">distance    -0.9179038 0.1844411</font></font></font