    [
     3,
     "<div>\r\n<div>On Feb 28 2020, at 11:50 pm, mitchfirman &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">mitchel...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:</div>\r\n</div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div><blockquote>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>Greetings List,</div>\r\n<div><br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>I&#39;m working on some aerial survey data for marine mammals with independent observers. Is there a limit to which the MR model will deal with poor observer performance?  In this situation, the primary observers are experienced professionals and the secondary\r\n observers are locals. When I look at the graphs depicting observer performance (e.g. objects detected by either observer compared to observer x, for binned distances) the primary observer performance looks great while the secondary is lacking: 444 obs by primary,\r\n 114 obs by secondary and 85 by both. When I run the analysis, the MR model assigns a similar dismal probability of detection to both observers (~0.30 each and ~0.50 combined). Is the poor secondary observer performance precluding the use of this data for MR\r\n analysis?  As a 0.30 detection probability is unlikely for the primary observer (as evidenced by other survey data), it would appear that the MR analysis will give the data a positive bias? Is there a &#39;rule of thumb&#39; to assess observer performance when using\r\n MR analysis?</div>\r\n<div><br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>Thanks in advance,</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>Mitch Firman  </div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n</blockquote></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div><blockquote><div>--</div>\r\n<div>You received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;distance-sampling&quot; group.</div>\r\n<div>To unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to\r\n<a href title=\"mailto:distance-sampling+unsubscribe@googlegroups.com\" data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">\r\ndistance-sampl...@googlegroups.com</a>.</div>\r\n<div>To view this discussion on the web visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/distance-sampling/592d20f5-bd6f-45e0-8ae0-310c10e8a54a%40googlegroups.com?utm_medium=email&amp;utm_source=footer\" title=\"https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/distance-sampling/592d20f5-bd6f-45e0-8ae0-310c10e8a54a%40googlegroups.com?utm_medium=email&amp;utm_source=footer\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/distance-sampling/592d20f5-bd6f-45e0-8ae0-310c10e8a54a%2540googlegroups.com?utm_medium%3Demail%26utm_source%3Dfooter&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792473517542000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3dBBZeitZq6UGQyIkZDoqn\">\r\nhttps://groups.google.com/d/msgid/distance-sampling/592d20f5-bd6f-45e0-8ae0-310c10e8a54a%40googlegroups.com</a>.</div>\r\n</blockquote>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n"
    ]
   ]
